Third-party code included in CORVID
===================================

This file states WHAT is third-party and WHERE it came from.
The licence texts those origins require are in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES, which is
the file that must ship with every binary release.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
No third-party source code
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

CORVID compiles no third-party source. Its sparse direct solves use SPARTA
(Copyright (C) 2026 Robert Fennis and Milan Rother, AGPL-3.0-or-later), linked
as a Rust crate. The other Rust crates CORVID links are listed with their
licences in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES. NumPy, SciPy and (off Apple) scipy-openblas32
are Python dependencies, installed separately and not distributed with CORVID;
corvid/_blas.py loads that OpenBLAS at run time, following SPARTA's
sparta/_blas.py.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Algorithms followed, with no code taken
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  Arnold, Falk & Winther       vertex-patch (Arnold-Falk-Winther) Schwarz
                               smoothing for H(curl): Multigrid in H(div) and
                               H(curl), Numer. Math. 85 (2000) 197-217.
                               src/patch.rs.

  Phillips & Fischer           fourth-kind Chebyshev smoothing: Optimal
                               Chebyshev smoothers and one-sided V-cycles,
                               arXiv:2210.03179 (2022). src/precond.rs.

  Hiptmair                     distributive (hybrid) smoothing on the gradient
                               space: Multigrid method for Maxwell's equations,
                               SIAM J. Numer. Anal. 36 (1998) 204-225. Research
                               path only (PSolver, research/).

  Pasciak & Vassilevski        exact de Rham sequences on agglomerated
                               elements: Exact de Rham sequences of spaces
                               defined on macro-elements in two and three
                               spatial dimensions, SIAM J. Sci. Comput. 30
                               (2008) 2427-2446. The design of LLNL's parELAG
                               library was followed; no parELAG code is used.
                               corvid/amge/.

  Palace (AWS Labs)            the structure of the p-multigrid preconditioner
                               with Chebyshev smoothing and a power-iteration
                               spectral estimate follows Palace's design. No
                               Palace code is used.

  van der Vorst & Melissen     COCG for complex symmetric systems: IEEE Trans.
                               Magn. 26 (1990) 706-708. src/krylov.rs.

  Saad & Schultz               GMRES: SIAM J. Sci. Stat. Comput. 7 (1986)
                               856-869. src/krylov.rs.

  Tinney & Walker; George & Liu  minimum-degree ordering of the vertex blocks:
                               Proc. IEEE 55 (1967); Computer Solution of Large
                               Sparse Positive Definite Systems (1981).
                               src/patch.rs.

